window.docContents[21].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.ModelIface/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___ModelIface":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Game › ModelIface.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 155 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nThe model interface Σ_model^H and the KeyInd experiment over a chosen handshakeTrusted: the statement. Read with Computational/Specifications/Game/GenericGame.lean and Computational/Specifications/Reductions/Pqxdh/StatementPqReds.lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Lemma 3 (ModelSecure, Computational/Specifications/Composition/StatementModel.lean) is stated over an arbitrary handshake, represented as a KeyInd oracle handler ki : QueryImpl (SignalPqxdh.keyIndSpec S) (StateT (SignalPqxdh.KeyIndState S) ProbComp) (the paper's H). This file defines the KeyInd game over ki and the composed-game interface modelIface (Σ_model^H), which runs ki followed by the byte-level Double Ratchet + SPQR session model on GhostState Bytes.\n\n\n\nKeyInd experiment over ki\n\ndef pqxdhKeyIndExpForHandshakeL44–59 ↗#PQXDH KeyInd experiment over an arbitrary KeyInd handler ki: samples a challenge bit secb, runs A against ki from KeyIndState.empty S secb, and returns a uniform bit if allTestedSessionsFresh P fails at game end or (b' == secb) otherwise.\n\ndef KeyIndAdvantageForHandshakeL61–66 ↗#Distinguishing advantage 2 |Pr[win] - 1/2| (boolBias) of A in pqxdhKeyIndExpForHandshake S P ki A.\n\nModel-state E2E driver\n\ndef bhE2EDrvImplWithL70–103 ↗#Model-state E2E driver over BHE2EDrvState S ℓ parameterized by the handshake handler ki: forwards KeyInd queries allowed by bhDrvKiQueryOk (refusing corruptIK u while u responds to a promoted no-OPK instance via bhNoOpkRespPromoted) and mirrors responses via bhE2EMirror, promotes sessions on startDR via compositionLocalStart ki, and steps promoted instances via bhE2EStepLocalSm.\n\n\n\nModel interface\n\ndef flattenImplL111–116 ↗#Lift a StateT D M query implementation to StateT D (StateT K M) via lens get / set.\n\ndef modelReassocL118–131 ↗#Reassociate composedSpec S ℓ (GhostState Bytes) into unifSpec + bhTargetGameSpec S ℓ (BitVec 512).\n\ndef modelAdvRunL133–156 ↗#\n\ndef modelIfaceL137–151 ↗#Model interface Σ_model^H of G(Σ) over handshake handler ki, primitives P, session crypto C, SPQR KEM K, and epoch cap qep, with leaked party state GhostState Bytes, challenge bit in BHE2EDrvState.b, and KeyInd state mirrored in BHE2EDrvState.st from KeyIndState.empty S true.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Game/ModelIface.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.ModelIface/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___ModelIface"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.FSAEAD.HybridWith/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___FSAEAD___HybridWith":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/FSAEAD › HybridWith.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 8 of 332 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nHybrid games and reductions of ACD19 Thm 5, with an AD-dependent ideal ciphertextTrusted in part. The CLI security theorems (Theorems/Main.lean under Computational/, Oom/Supporting.lean under Computational/Proofs/LibsignalCli/) use only IndexedOtccaSpec and slotToHybridHopIndex from this file: read them. The rest is used by no theorem of Computational/Theorems/. The Thm 5 hybrids and reductions among it are part of the statement of theorem5: read them to trust it. Every proof is checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Hybrid encrypting oracle (encIdxWith, otOpsWith), (ℕ × AD)-indexed OT-CCA interface (IndexedOtccaSpec, IndexedOtccaState, otImpl), multi-slot OT-CCA reduction (multiSlotOtccaReduction), and hop-index encoding (slotToHybridHopIndex) with AD-dependent ideal ciphertexts ideal (i, a) (DEV-FS17).\n\n\n\nnotation \"St\"L47 ↗#\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 49–82): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.encIdxWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.otOpsWith\n\nabbrev IndexedOtccaSpecL94–95 ↗#(ℕ × AD)-indexed OT-CCA oracle interface (uniform coins plus encrypt/decrypt).\n\n17 declarations not shown (lines 97–322): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.IndexedOtccaState, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.otImpl, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiKind, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiDecIdx, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiEncIdxWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiReceiveH, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiDeliverH, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiInjectH, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiTransmitHWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiChallengeHWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiOraclesWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiImplWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiRunWith, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.multiSlotOtccaReduction, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.sampleKeys, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.initOStM, CryptoGames.FSAEAD.Thm5.slotRedImpl\n\ndef slotToHybridHopIndexL324–329 ↗#Map slot j < 2 * q + (maxSkip + 1) to its encoded hybrid hop index m, which the single-slot reductions decode into chain position m / 2 and lookahead bit isLookaheadHop m = (m % 2 == 1):* for j < 2 * q, slotToHybridHopIndex q j = j (interleaving 2 * k and 2 * k + 1 for k < q);* for j = 2 * q + d, slotToHybridHopIndex q j = 2 * (q + d) + 1 (the remaining lookahead hops k ≥ q).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/FSAEAD/HybridWith.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.FSAEAD.HybridWith/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___FSAEAD___HybridWith"}});